<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Roundtree is a 51-year-old man with stage IIA, hormone receptor-positive, HER2-negative left breast cancer, treated by mastectomy and axillary dissection three weeks ago, who comes for his periodic preventive visit before chemotherapy starts next week. The scar is healed and he has nearly full movement of the left shoulder; the numbness under the left arm is unchanged. His echocardiogram four days ago was normal. The germline test result is not back yet. He is sleeping well, is back at the gym with light lower-body work, and has told only a few close friends about the diagnosis. He no longer needs pain medicine and has no fever, cough, or bone pain. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, timed before chemotherapy</td></tr><tr><td>Active conditions</td><td>Left breast cancer, stage IIA, after surgery; chemotherapy to start next week</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>None regularly; finished acetaminophen ten days ago</td></tr><tr><td>Recent results</td><td>Echocardiogram normal (ejection fraction 62 percent); germline panel pending</td></tr><tr><td>Functional status</td><td>Independent; light training; working</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient before the visit and reviewed during the visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good, apart from the cancer</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Worried about how chemotherapy will affect his work and appearance; close friends aware; wants the diagnosis kept private at work</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol and drugs</td><td>Two or three drinks a week (AUDIT-C 2); no other drug use</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Runs and trains most days before surgery; light training now</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Regular meals; high protein; no supplements</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Seven hours a night</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>No concerns before treatment; fertility and sexual effects of chemotherapy discussed with oncology</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>Wears a seat belt; smoke detectors at home; no firearms in the home</td></tr><tr><td>Oral health</td><td>No dental visit in the past year</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>No concerns; eye examination last year</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

