<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed</content>. Preventive care brought up to date before chemotherapy. Total cholesterol 186, HDL 56, LDL 112 mg/dL; HbA1c 5.3 percent; ten-year cardiovascular risk about 4 percent. [S]<list><item>Vaccines given today, at least five days before the first cycle.</item><item>Next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Left breast cancer, stage IIA, after mastectomy and axillary dissection (C50.122)</content>. Recovering well; ready for chemotherapy. Hepatitis B screening is needed before chemotherapy, and a dental check is advised before it starts. [S]<list><item>Hepatitis B surface antigen, core antibody, and surface antibody drawn today for medical oncology to review before cycle 1.</item><item>Dental appointment booked for this week.</item><item>Medical oncology to review the germline result when it is back.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Influenza vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Inactivated vaccine given today; a live vaccine is not used with chemotherapy</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine, this season</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Given today, before chemotherapy</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today; recommended at 50 and older, and before chemotherapy</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Recommended at 50 and older; to be given after chemotherapy, when the response will be better, unless oncology advises giving it during treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening and vaccination</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Triple panel drawn today, as recommended for all adults and before chemotherapy; vaccination if not immune</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C and HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>One-time screening recommended for all adults; no prior result; drawn with his consent today</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis booster</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap five years ago</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>124/78 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Cholesterol screening and statin decision</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Total cholesterol 186, HDL 56, LDL 112 mg/dL; ten-year risk about 4 percent with no diabetes, hypertension, or smoking, so a statin is not recommended</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>HbA1c 5.3 percent; also a baseline before dexamethasone with chemotherapy</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Due</td><td>Due from 45; no screening on record. A colonoscopy or a stool test will be arranged after chemotherapy</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Shared decision-making about PSA testing is recommended from 55. If the germline panel shows a BRCA2 variant, screening would start now</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer and abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Never used tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 score 1; PHQ-9 6 last week</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>AUDIT-C score 2; advised to avoid alcohol in the days around each chemotherapy cycle</td></tr><tr><td>Dental examination</td><td>Referred</td><td>No dental visit in the past year; a check before chemotherapy is advised; booked this week</td></tr><tr><td>Eye examination</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Last year</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, 2026-2027 season (inactivated); COVID-19 mRNA vaccine, 2026-2027 formula; Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, breast cancer monograph (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: First chemotherapy cycle next week with medical oncology. Hepatitis B, hepatitis C, and HIV results to oncology before cycle 1. Dental visit this week. Primary care review during chemotherapy, after the second cycle. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
